# Interactive MRI Signal Contrast & Physics Simulator

An interactive, browser-based simulator demonstrating structural tissue contrast dynamics using the steady-state Gradient-Echo signal equation. Built specifically as a teaching tool for medical imaging physicists, radiologists, and MRI technologists.

## Live Application
👉 https://mriphysicssimilation-qt3jo2boxrmqtrfcjgbzhe.streamlit.app/

## Core Features
* **Anatomical Brain Phantom:** A synthetic matrix modeling White Matter, Gray Matter, and CSF structural environments.
* **Real-Time Physics Engine:** Employs the steady-state Ernst Angle math loops to render tissue interactions natively.
* **One-Click Clinical Presets:** Instantly snap sliders into standard **T1-Weighted**, **T2-Weighted**, and **Proton Density (PD)** configurations.
* **Simultaneous Graph Tracking:** View longitudinal recovery vectors and transverse decay lines update side-by-side with the image matrix.

## ⚙️ Mathematical Framework
Tissue signal intensities ($S$) are calculated using the sequence equation:

$$S = \rho \cdot \frac{\sin(\alpha) \cdot (1 - e^{-TR/T1})}{1 - \cos(\alpha) \cdot e^{-TR/T1}} \cdot e^{-TE/T2}$$

## 🛠️ Technology Stack
* Python 3
* Streamlit (UI Framework)
* NumPy (Matrix Calculations)
* Matplotlib (Image & Graph Rendering)
